  
1200 Problem:-
Given an array of distinct integers arr, find all pairs of elements with the minimum absolute difference of any two elements.
Return a list of pairs in ascending order(with respect to pairs), each pair [a, b] follows
a, b are from arr
a < b
b - a equals to the minimum absolute difference of any two elements in arr
 
Example 1:
Input: arr = [4,2,1,3]
Output: [[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]]
Explanation: The minimum absolute difference is 1. List all pairs with difference equal to 1 in ascending order.

Example 2:
Input: arr = [1,3,6,10,15]
Output: [[1,3]]

Example 3:
Input: arr = [3,8,-10,23,19,-4,-14,27]
Output: [[-14,-10],[19,23],[23,27]]
 
Constraints:
2 <= arr.length <= 105
-106 <= arr[i] <= 106

====================================================================================================================================================================================

Solution:-
Intuition:-
Think about this, for a small number 1, what number do we take to minimize the absolute difference of both pair?
Taking the 1000 or 999 will yield a very large difference.
But taking the smaller number 2 yield a the minimum difference of 1.
Hence, to minimize the absolute difference of pairs sum, the smallest element must pair with another element:
Pairing with the largest number produces the maximum difference.
Otherwise, pairing with the next greater number produces the minimum difference.

Algorithm:-
Here, we pair 1 element with the next greater element 3:
We take its difference and set this as the current minimum difference, as well we set the temporary result (as the index of 1 for simplicity).
After 1 is paired, we can safely ignore this, since each element can only belong to one pair.
Now, 3 is the smallest and 4 is the next greater number.
We have a new current minimum difference of 1.
That means, we have to reset the temporary result as the index of 3 (the new minimum).

Contuining the process...
In this pair, the difference is 3, but the minimum is 1:
Thus, we wont record this to the result:
For the final pair:
Hence, the correspoding pairs with Minimum Absolute Difference are:
res=[5[3,4], 2[4,5], 4[8,9]]

Sorting:-
To make the process more efficient:
We can sort the array in ascending order to directly access the next greater element.
Then follow the same process for finding the result.

Time Complexity: O(nlogn)
Space Complexity: O(n)

Code:-
class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> minimumAbsDifference(int[] A) {
        Arrays.sort(A);
        int n = A.length;
        int minDiff = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        List<List<Integer>> res = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            int diff = A[i] - A[i - 1];
            if (diff < minDiff) {
                minDiff = diff;
                res = new ArrayList<>();
                res.add(Arrays.asList(A[i - 1], A[i]));
            } else if (diff == minDiff) {
                res.add(Arrays.asList(A[i - 1], A[i]));
            }
        }

        return res;
    }
}
